id: pmc-ie8u
title: Keep published dependency updates in the generated changelog
description: Pass the dependency updates flag through the package changelog entry points so regeneration preserves published dependency bullets.
type: Chore
status: in_progress
priority: 2
tags[2]: changelog,maintenance
created_at: "2026-11-24T05:51:19.511Z"
updated_at: "2026-11-24T06:00:03.376Z"
author: codex-agent
estimated_minutes: 30
acceptance_criteria: Every changelog entry point uses dependency updates. Removing the flag from any entry point fails the regression.
comments[2]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-11-24T05:51:27.617Z",codex-agent,"The project generator already passes the flag. Add it to release:notes, and guard the built CLI, the project generator, and both package scripts that delegate to it."
  "2026-11-24T05:59:59.961Z",codex-agent,"Full regeneration kept all 62 published dependency bullets and restored 0 versus main. Removing the project generator flag omitted 53 published bullets. Removing the flag from release:notes or the project generator separately fails the regression. Bypassing the generator from either changelog:full or changelog:check also fails. The regression passed after restoration, and typecheck, docstring, build, and 119 focused tests passed. The local release notes gate uses a scratch GitHub step summary file."
